BND-19: report inflow volumes for the reporting period when REPORT_START is late

The Node Inflow "Total Inflow Volume", the Outfall Loading "Total Volume"
and the denominators of the storage "% Evap/Exfil Loss" printed massbal's
NodeInflow[], which accumulates from START, next to statistics that
stats_updateFlowStats() collects only from REPORT_START. On the first
statistics step of a late reporting period, store each node's NodeInflow in
the new TNodeStats field inflowBeforeRpt and subtract it in those columns.
The flow balance error column still uses the whole run. When reporting
starts with the run the field stays 0 and the report is unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply BND-19_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/objects.h b/src/legacy/engine/objects.h
index 6b54d76..64a1952 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/objects.h
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/objects.h
@@ -1018,6 +1018,7 @@ typedef struct
    int           nonConvergedCount;
    DateTime      maxInflowDate;
    DateTime      maxOverflowDate;
+   double        inflowBeforeRpt;    // inflow volume before reporting began (ft3)
 }  TNodeStats;
 
 //-------------------
diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/stats.c b/src/legacy/engine/stats.c
index 6d38f70..a1ce9d4 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/stats.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/stats.c
@@ -446,6 +446,14 @@ void stats_updateFlowStats(double tStep, DateTime aDate)
     if ( aDate < ReportStart ) return;
     SysOutfallFlow = 0.0;
 
+    // --- if reporting starts after the simulation does, note the inflow
+    //     volume each node received before it (NodeInflow covers the run)
+    if ( ReportStepCount == 0 && ReportStart > StartDateTime )
+    {
+        for ( j=0; j<Nobjects[NODE]; j++ )
+            NodeStats[j].inflowBeforeRpt = NodeInflow[j];
+    }
+
     // --- update node & link stats
 //#pragma omp parallel num_threads(NumThreads)
 {
